    "body": "### Problem\n\nAdding multiple cursors and doing actions that involve adding new lines may cause undos to not correctly reflect the original state.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. Add the following text to the buffer\n```\ntest1\ntest2\ntest1\ntest2\ntest1\ntest2\n```\n2. Search for test1 using `/test1`.\n3. Add multicursors using `1Q`.\n4. Add something to the end of the line and press enter`A{<CR>`.\n5. Go back to normal mode and press undo `<Esc>u`.\n6. The buffer is now\n```\ntest1\n\ntest1\ntest1{\ntest1\ntest2\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe undo should result in the following text.\n```\ntest1\ntest2\ntest1\ntest2\ntest1\ntest2\n```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1583+g d039f19af5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 15.7.7\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\ngithub download",
